Now it is clear, that path through the lilac plants is lethal, so you have no other option, but to make your way through the thick shrubs of white flower bushes. It's not an easy task to go through them, but reliable machete helps to clear the way. Your efforts turn out well, and soon through gaps between bushes you see the water body.  
Finally, last bushes fall under your pressure, and with a sense of relief you step on the silty shore of the lake, leaving thick shrubberies behind.